msgid "There's also a glossary button in the top right corner if you want more explanation on what each means!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/24
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Anything else you'd like to know?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Any other SPECS questions?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do I get more SPECS?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Are SPECS choices in dialogue always good?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do I know which dateable gives which SPECS points?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/3/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'm good on SPECS!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Any time there's a first-time change in relationship between you and a dateable object, you will be rewarded with 5 SPECS points in one attribute!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Think of it as you growing in experience dating a vast array of personalities, each with something to give you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-0/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But don't think you can just keep switching between relationship statuses on the same object over and over again to get a lot of points..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-0/31
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Only the <i>first</i> time there's a change from neutral will there be any SPECS awarded."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "They are! Or at the very least, you get something fun out of it!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-1/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But don't worry if you can't reach a certain SPECS dialogue choice - the worst thing that you could miss out on is a collectable."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-1/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "No Love, Friend, or Hate endings are gated behind a SPECS check."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Great question!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-2/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Each dateable object gives out <i>one</i> SPECS attribute when a relationship has been attained - I call this \"Alignment\"."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-2/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You can check a dateable's Alignment by looking at the SPECS badge in their date-a-dex page."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-2/31
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "The badge corresponds to which stat is given!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-2/39
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "If you're looking to grow to a certain SPECS build... this will really help guide you towards who you should prioritize."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/specs_explain/0/33/8/c-2/47/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Y'know, for Realization Recipes!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Collectables are the funny little images that appear as dateables talk to you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "What are you curious about?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Any other collectables questions?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What do they do?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How many are there?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Do I get anything for collecting all of them?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/3/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'm good on collectables!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "They help illustrate what's going on around you - sometimes for fun, sometimes because the dateable gave you an item, or sometimes just for dramatic effect!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Think of them as little progress trinkets. You can take a closer look at them in the date-a-dex sorted by character!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "A lot..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-1/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Each dateable has at least three to give out."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-1/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But one has up to 33!!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-1/31
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That's... way too many."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well, of course there's an achievement. What are you thinking, man?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/18
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But honestly, I don't care very much if you find them all."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/26
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "They're just there to give a little extra flavor to everything!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/34
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I'm here to help you forge new relationships."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "All right, I'll focus on the dateables then."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "But I love collecting things!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Can I get them all in one playthrough?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Awesome!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I won't stop you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "No, unfortunately that's not possible."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/c-2/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "At a minimum, it would take 3 whole playthroughs to find them all."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/collectables_explain/0/17/8/c-2/45/c-2/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Fortunately, New Game+ tracks your collectable collecting progress!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "A very important question..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "The easy answer is... whatever you like!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/16/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "As long as you are continuing to awaken objects, things will continue to move along in a positive direction."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/17/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "As long as you are continuing to Realize objects, things will continue to move along in a positive direction."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/20/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Even with how many Hate endings you have, you'll still be able to do some form of good in the world..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/20/b/9
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "If you even want that..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "If you have other questions, I'm all ears."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Any other questions about what you should be doing?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Can a bad ending with someone 'lock me out' of finding another?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "When should I leave the house?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Is there anything wrong with getting Hate endings?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/3/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'm good on strategy!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "No matter what you do, you will always be able to find every single dateable here!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Except for one <i>very specific instance</i>, but you will be very clearly warned that that's the path you're going on!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'll be on the lookout!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'll still be sure to fuck it up."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Can you give me a hint what that instance is?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/3/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Oh shit, I did that I think!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-1/7/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "No... I believe in you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-1/8/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Yeah, you probably will you little shit."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well... it'll be if you refuse to go on a certain subterranean quest."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-2/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That's all I'll say!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-3/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Welp. There you go."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-3/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You won't be able to find everybody in this particular playthrough. Womp Womp."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-3/23/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Eh, whatever. Beau talked too much."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-3/23/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Darn!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-3/23/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Hm. You're not wrong."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-0/23/c-3/23/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's okay, you're not locked out of any good endings, regardless."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You can leave the house at any time... but be forewarned."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Doing that starts the end of your story. A point of no return..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "<i>Unless of course, you reload a save. Wink, wink.</i>"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do I know when I'm ready to leave the house in your opinion?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do I get the best endings?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "If you want the barest minimum of a good ending, I would shoot to get 100 SPECS points in any one attribute."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Once you have that - you'll get some pretty good results!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/c-1/7 skylar_specs/skylar_hello_1/0/c-2/15 skylar_specs/skylar_hello_2/0/g-0/c-4/21/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/c-1/15/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I would recommend getting to know all the dateable objects. That will really help."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-1/31/c-1/16/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Try to Realize as many objects as you can! Once you're in the 90s, you're good to go!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Hate endings still give you 5 SPECS points and continue the main story, so nah, not really."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You won't be locked out of very much, except for certain polyamorous relationships that might be difficult to untangle if you were looking for those ones specifically."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/23/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But, since you won't be able to Realize objects that Hate you, you might start to find yourself locked out of certain endings if you keep getting a large amount of Hates!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/26
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Just speak with everyone honestly - from the heart! You don't have to literally get <i>everyone</i> to be your lover. Seriously!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/34
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Even though it makes me happy - there's no pressure at all."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/42
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "If anything, getting something to hate you certainly does mean you spend less time talking with them, which is always good if you genuinely don't like them!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/strategy_explain/0/32/8/c-2/50/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Isn't that right, you sonofabitch?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "What do you want to know about my lore?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Anything else you want to know about me and my beautiful Suspension?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "No lore for me, I'm full!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do the dateviators work in the first place?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do dateables talk to each other?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/3/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Why is there no real-world stuff and everything is a thing-based pun?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/4/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How do dateables eat, listen to music, etc.?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/5/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "When I love a thing, what physically am I doing?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/6/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What's so special about this house?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/7/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Why is everyone so attractive?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/8/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Is one door all doors? Is one table all tables?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/9/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "How are you able to bring objects to life?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/10/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What happens when a Realized object dies?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/11/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What happens if I use the dateviators on a human?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/12/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Guess there's nothing more to ask..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/lore_menu/0/9/8/c-12/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That's all I got for now! Thanks for your curiosity!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Vibrations."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/8/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That's it?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/9/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Okay, makes sense, moving on..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Wait wait wait wait wait!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I'm being overly simplistic."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Have you ever heard of String Theory?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Yeah."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "No... is that bad?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/18/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Can you date string??"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/c-3/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Not bad at all! It's just a model for how matter might be constructed. First theorized in the 1960s."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/c-4/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "No, it's too small a constituent part."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-0/c-4/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Think of how when you speak to a person, you speak to their whole discrete being, even though they really are just a big ol' collection of cells."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-1/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Dateviator technology is based on <i>Thing Theory.</i>"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-1/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Thing Theory theorizes that at large enough scales, all objects and concepts coalesce into their own one-dimensional wavelength that unifies all of that type of object throughout the universe!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-1/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "You're losing my interest..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-1/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Intriguing..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-1/c-5/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "No worries! I'll dumb it down. (no i wont)."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Any object that makes up any specific wavelength is connected to all other objects on that wavelength - which by virtue of being complex enough then forms a gestalt consciousness."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Humans just never had a way of speaking with those consciousnesses until now!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What's 'gestalt'?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'm tapping out!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "When the whole becomes more than the sum of its parts!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "With objects, it happens as a plank of wood slowly becomes a toy boat - the wood didn't change, but its status did."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "And once it's more toy boat than plank of wood, it changes its wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/31
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Its thing-ness is vibrating differently enough to find a new 'signal' - or 'spin'."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/39/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "So when does each separate wavelength form?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/39/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Once the object or idea becomes large enough to have its own state, it breaks off the wavelength and forms a new one."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/39/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That's why tables are different than chairs, even though they might be both made from wood."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-7/39/c-0/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Their thing-ness is vibrating differently enough to find a new 'signal' - or 'spin'."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-2/c-8/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That's okay!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-3/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I like to call the wavelengths 'animus', but you can use any term, really."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-3/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "This is how we can Directly Acknowledge these Things' Existences!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_1/0/g-3/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Dateviators vibrate along each of these 'anima'! That's why when we awaken something it wiggles a little!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I'll be honest..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "We're not speaking English right now."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Oh no, one of these."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What? Japanese or something?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/18/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Wow!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's true, though!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Nah, ya know, not quite..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "The speeds at which objects and concepts think is both faster and slower than the rate at which humans think and speak."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Faster in that the objects have instantaneous consciousness throughout their different forms in the universe..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "And slower in that the timelines for them can stretch into eons..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/24
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "All that to say, part of my job is making sure that we can all understand each other."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/32
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Which means I'm processing their speech and rate of thought at a completely different timeline than yours!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/40
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "So necessarily... we're not <i>really</i> talking in English..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/48/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That's okay... as long as I can still understand it!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/49/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Bzxrchshsrxr sas r er rc."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/50/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Can I ever learn to speak their language?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/c-4/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I mean, that's still coming up as gibberish on my end so all good."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_2/0/g-0/c-5/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Maybe... one day I can teach you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Wait... what do you mean 'real-world'?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/8/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'm used to everything around me not always having an object ham-fisted into its name."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Huh."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well I'm not sure what to say except to give a brief history of the world that <i>you</i> live in..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Which you should already know about, but you know, heheh, I'm here for you."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Pretend I don't know."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Humans love objects... always have."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But even more so in today's hyper-commercialized society."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Recently TV shows, books, and ordinary brand names have been making the switch to incorporating a focus on making products and entertainment more thing-based in order to drive up sales."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/31
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "And you might even recognize some historical names with some objects added to them."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/39
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "All for brand potential."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Why would historical people have become branded?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/1/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Perfect - I love things, and I love buying them too!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/2/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Except Shakespeare."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Someone's gotta make that money, honey."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "The more things in the world, the more things to love!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/c-1/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "...right?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_3/0/c-0/31/c-0/47/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Yeah except Shakespeare."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's true... they really do act like humans!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "With human emotions, desires, and appetites too."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "What's happening is that there's a whole other dimension to these animus wavelengths than even we can be completely aware of."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/24
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Objects and concepts have these rich inner lives that we can't see at all in our dimension."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/32
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Somehow they are able to have jobs, marriages, kids... but we can only see what's right in front of us."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/40
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Even me with my vibrational qualities! I can only be a part of the process just for the bit that I see."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/48/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "So you're telling me you don't know?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I don't... really know."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Because I can't see all of it..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/c-0/23/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Hm. Maybe it's all a bit lost in translation?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/c-0/23/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "They could have lives parallel to the ones humans have, and we just can't sense it precisely?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_4/0/c-0/23/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Maybe..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "When a dateable object falls in love with you, it might speak to you in terms of what a human might think of as 'sex'."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's not."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's more that your two consciousnesses are intertwining in the vibrational aether caused by the focus of my lenses."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/24
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Basically, you're not having sex with your furniture."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/32/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well, until you Realize them. Then you can do whatever freaky stuff you want..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/35/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What if I want to have sex with my furniture?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/36/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Okay, I'm kinda relieved honestly."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/37/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Hmm... all right."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You can do that on your own time. I don't need to see that."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_5/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Good."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Honestly, nothing!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Aside from some traces of some previous owners who I have to keep secret..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What was that??"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Keep your secrets, then..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "T-t-t-the time isn't right!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Since we have the only pair of dateviators in existence, there is certainly quite the buzz in the object and concept world!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/g-0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "There's a whole lot of vibrating going on! Feel it?! Yeeeaahhh!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/g-0/19/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "But they always seem to talk about me specifically. Am I more special than my neighbors?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/g-0/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "They are always aware of their other forms in other places, for sure."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/g-0/c-2/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But that doesn't mean that the ones in this house are any less or more conscious."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_6/0/g-0/c-2/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "A table leg never forgets... no matter where it is."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Aw... thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/8/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "You are!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/9/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I meant the others."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Always nice to hear..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Jeez, harsh."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Honestly, the reason is that I can shape anyone into whatever form I want!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Sure there are quite a few who other humans might call 'hotties'..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But it's just my best representation of what they are in total!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "So, you're an artist?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "<i>hairflip</i> It's true... And I think I have a very good artistic eye."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/c-2/15/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Well, thanks for that then!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_7/0/g-0/c-2/15/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Yes, each object is the same from all corners of the universe."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Once the form of each object took shape, say 'microwave', the animus of its carrier was born."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/16/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Luke Nukem, as you know."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/17/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You don't know him yet, but his name is Luke."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/17/b/12
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Luke Nukem."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/20
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "There might be deviations between ones around the world, but once the metal and circuits become a microwave, it then vibrates along Luke's very own wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/28/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "What happens if all microwaves were destroyed, or forgotten?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/29/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I've seen different forms of the same dateable object..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "An animus can leave a skeleton of itself once the concept has gone away..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "In this way, objects and concepts can 'die'..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/c-0/23
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "But they can always be resurrected if someone comes along and reconstructs it somewhere..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's true - there are several Dorians for example, even here."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_8/0/c-1/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Sometimes, it's just fun to put on a costume!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Realization is possible when the object is giving off so much positive energy from feeling loved or becoming a good friend that I'm able to really easily 'hook in' to their animus!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "If this is then paired with an exceptional wearer of the dateviators who has the same potential SPECS energy to complete the circuit..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I can mold the animus vibrations to make a real human!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/24
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Or at least, a really close approximation of one."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/32/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Wait, so they aren't humans?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/33/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Close enough for me."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "They will always have their own vibrations underneath..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_9/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Good! If it looks like a duck, and quacks like a duck... quack, quack, right?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I'm relieved you asked - because it certainly does seem problematic on the surface!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Bring these objects to life, only to have them eventually die??"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Yeah, these are the kinda problems I face."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "It does seem a little strange."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "All part of being human..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "I'll explain."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "When I'm Realizing an object, I'm not really transferring all of their animus to an existing human body, or creating any real 'flesh'."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "It's more that I'm molding the animus around us into a very lifelike human substitute that follows practically every human feature you're familiar with."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Like, a really good veggie burger!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I love veggie burgers!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I don't like talking about flesh like this..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/26/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Human substitutes... I guess that makes sense?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Sure whatever!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-0/c-3/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "You asked... I'm answerin'!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-1/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "When the Realized object passes away eventually, the animus simply resolves back into its original form."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_10/0/g-1/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That even means there's no corpse or anything. Pretty neat, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well... since we now know that objects have consciousness just as rich and worldly as humans do..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/8
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That means that humans themselves are part of their own unified animus."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/16
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "The implications are..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That we're all just 'Humy the Human'?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Bewildering..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/26/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That I'm part of my own wavelength called the"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/26/s/5
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "animus..."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Well, more that you're all more interconnected than you think."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/c-0/15
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "That's why spreading Love around is the most important thing to me."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Yep."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/c-2/7
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Ooooo, that's an interesting interpretation... huuh?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/skylar_lore_11/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Either way, we won't know until we step outside."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/0
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "What do you think about that?"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/8/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I think that makes perfect sense!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/9/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "It's a lot to take in... but I believe it."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/10/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Honestly? Needs a little work."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/11/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That's ridiculous."
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/c-0/7/b/1 skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/c-1/7/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Whew! What a relief!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/c-0/8/b/1 skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/c-1/8/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Yes! Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/c-0/9/b/1 skylar_specs/after_lore_sorter/0/c-1/9/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Nice! Thank you!"
msgstr ""

